  "glow_from": "MoveObject's per-type case for object 117, by way of the old port's own table. The client animates the self-luminous submesh alone and not through the model's skeleton: BlendMeshLight scales its brightness and BlendMeshTexCoordV slides its texture, both off the world clock, so every placement of a type moves in step.\n\nThat 'in step' is what makes it cheap \u2014 the glow of a type is one material shared by every placement, so it costs one material write a frame however many stand in the town.\n\nA candle behind dirty glass, which neither jumps nor sits still. Both numbers do opposite jobs. Eight draws a second rather than three and a half keeps the glow always on its way somewhere; at the slower rate it arrived, waited visibly, then set off again, which is what read as a flicker. A third of a second to travel rather than a fifth means it never arrives before the next draw. Twelve steps rather than four, because four quantises the range into levels you can count.",
